\begin_layout Subsection

\lang british
Constrained kinematic controller
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang british
Once the plan 
\begin_inset Formula $(\pi_{\text{geom}},\mathcal{Y})$
\end_inset

 is successfully certified,
 the trajectory is executed using constrained kinematic controller.
 Considering a generalised vector of 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{\text{task}}\in\mathbb{N}$
\end_inset

 desired task variable 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{x}_{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{\text{task}}}$
\end_inset

,
 and the task error 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{\boldsymbol{x}}\triangleq\boldsymbol{x}-\boldsymbol{x}_{d}$
\end_inset

,
 this specific manipulation domain focuses strictly on end-effector translation control,
 and so 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{x}\triangleq\boldsymbol{t}(\boldsymbol{q})\in\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

,
 the desired target variable is 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{x}_{d}\triangleq\boldsymbol{t}_{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}$
\end_inset

,
 and the task tracking error is given by 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{\boldsymbol{x}}\triangleq\boldsymbol{t}(\boldsymbol{q})-\boldsymbol{t}_{d}$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "quiroz2019whole,marinho2019dynamic"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
 The control input 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{u}$
\end_inset

 is obtained from the following optimisation problem
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\argminimone{\boldsymbol{u}\in}{\dot{\boldsymbol{q}}}{\|\boldsymbol{J}\dot{\boldsymbol{q}}+\eta\tilde{\boldsymbol{x}}\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda\|\dot{\boldsymbol{q}}\|_{2}^{2}}{\boldsymbol{W}\dot{\boldsymbol{q}}\ensuremath{\preceq}\boldsymbol{w},}\label{eq:kinematic-controller}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{J}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times n}$
\end_inset

 is the task Jacobian,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}$
\end_inset

 is the joint configuration vector of 
\begin_inset Formula $n\in\mathbb{N}$
\end_inset

 joints,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\eta\in(0,\infty)$
\end_inset

 is the proportional gain determining the convergence rate of the closed-loop error,
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda\in(0,\infty)$
\end_inset

 is a damping factor penalising high joint velocities.
 Additionally,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n}$
\end_inset

 is the constraint matrix with 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{w}\triangleq\boldsymbol{w}(q)\in\mathbb{R}^{p}$
\end_inset

 enforces 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

 linear constraints on the control inputs,
 which are used to prevent joint limit violations and collisions via the Vector Field Inequalities framework 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "marinho2019dynamic"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
 These require the definition of distance functions between collidable entities and the corresponding distance Jacobians,
 enabling the robot to avoid restricted regions or remain safely within them.
 
\end_layout

