\begin_layout Subsubsection

\lang british
Inference time action masking
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang british
Geometric and kinematic failures are not handled by an online reward loop,
 they are recorded in a set of failures 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{F}^{(k)}$
\end_inset

.
 Before an action 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi_{t_{\text{step}}}\in\mathcal{A}$
\end_inset

 is sampled by the policy combines these constraints with the task planner.
 The masking layer sets the probability of all invalid actions at specific MDP state 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{s}_{t}$
\end_inset

 to zero and renormalises the remaining distribution
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
p_{\theta,\text{masked}}(\pi_{t_{\text{step}}}\mid s_{t_{\text{step}}})=\begin{cases}
0, & \text{if }\pi_{t_{\text{step}}}\in\mathcal{F}^{(k)},\\
\dfrac{p_{\theta}(\pi_{t_{\text{step}}}\mid s_{t_{\text{step}}})}{\sum_{\pi_{t_{\text{step}}}\notin\mathcal{F}^{(k)}}p_{\theta}(\pi_{t_{\text{step}}}\mid s_{t_{\text{step}}})} & \text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}\label{eq:inference-masking}
\end{equation}

\end_inset

Executing the masked policy until the goal is reached produces the task plan,
 that is the sequence of actions denoted 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathscr{\pi}_{\text{symbolic}}$
\end_inset

 such that
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\boldsymbol{\pi}_{\text{symbolic}}=(\pi_{1},\dots,\pi_{t_{\text{step}}})\label{eq:renewed-taskplan}
\end{equation}

\end_inset


\end_layout

